Place the PCB: 75x75 mm, 33 footprints, nets assigned, DRC clean

Adds pcb_layout.py, which drives the KiCad pcbnew API to build the board
from the same component table used for the schematic:

- Board outline 75x75 mm on Edge.Cuts and four M3 holes on the standard
  30.5x30.5 mm pattern. The side is chosen automatically as the smallest
  square where every footprint fits without invading a hole.
- Shelf packing with the holes as obstacles; the footprint bounding-box
  offset is honoured so boxes land exactly where computed (a previous
  attempt overlapped because the bbox is not centred on the origin).
- Nets created and assigned to every pad; value text hidden to keep the
  silkscreen clean.
- Footprint assignment added to the schematic generator (all 33 symbols
  now carry a footprint).

Validation: no bounding-box overlaps, nothing outside the outline, DRC
reports 0 violations. The 86 unconnected items are the unrouted tracks.

